Force the runtime-pseudo-reloc stub undef on aarch64-pc-cygwin shared links

ld synthesises the runtime-pseudo-reloc stub (*_ertr*.o) only AFTER it has
finished scanning archives, so the stub's fresh reference to
_pei386_runtime_relocator has no archive pass left to satisfy it and
pseudo-reloc-dummy.o is never pulled from libcygwin.a.  Every aarch64 shared
library that reads a data symbol from another DLL therefore fails to link:

  ld: liba_dll_ertr000001.o:(.rdata+0x0): undefined reference to
      `_pei386_runtime_relocator'

Placing the undef in the driver's LINK_SPEC makes the reference exist BEFORE
the scan, so the archive member is pulled.  This is the same arrangement the
native x86_64 target already gets (there via a .refptr resolved at link time).

The undef is gated on %{shared|mdll}, so executable links are unaffected.

This must go in gcc/config/aarch64/msys.h, NOT in i386/cygwin-w64.h:
config.gcc lists aarch64/msys.h LAST in tm_file for this target and that
header #undef's LINK_SPEC, so any LINK_SPEC written into cygwin-w64.h is
discarded.  Verify with `aarch64-pc-cygwin-gcc -dumpspecs | grep pei386` on the
built driver, not by reading the headers.

diff --git a/gcc/config/aarch64/msys.h b/gcc/config/aarch64/msys.h
index d104f34..237a023 100644
--- a/gcc/config/aarch64/msys.h
+++ b/gcc/config/aarch64/msys.h
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
      - DLL entry symbol  : _cygwin_dll_entry -> _msys_dll_entry
      - DLL search prefix : cyg              -> msys-
      - runtime import lib: -lcygwin         -> -lmsys-2.0
+     - shared links additionally force the pseudo-reloc stub undef (see below)
    The rest of the spec (subsystem, shared/dll, static/dynamic, -m aarch64pe via
    the base header's target) is preserved verbatim.  */
 
@@ -39,6 +40,7 @@
   %{shared|mdll: %{!m32:-e _msys_dll_entry} %{m32:-e __msys_dll_entry@12} --enable-auto-image-base} \
   %(shared_libgcc_undefs) \
   --dll-search-prefix=msys- \
+  %{shared|mdll: -u _pei386_runtime_relocator} \
   %{rdynamic: --export-all-symbols} \
   %{!shared: %{!mdll: %{m32:--large-address-aware} --tsaware}}"
 
